      "narrative": "Mara blinks at your question, a crease forming between her brows. \"Before it was *filed*?\" She repeats the word slowly, as if testing its fit. \"I don't follow. The lock's not filed, Kael. It's *jammed*. Nobody's filed anything.\"\n\nShe tilts her head, studying you with renewed curiosity \u2014 the kind a scholar gives a confusing footnote.\n\n\"Toran Vex built the whole assembly, lock included. He's the only one who's ever maintained it. Old Bram didn't know a wrench from a wine cork, and I sure as ashes didn't touch it before I started investigating. So unless you know something I don't about a secret third party...\"\n\nShe lets the sentence hang, waiting for you to clarify. Her thumb taps once against the mug.\n\n\"You're thinking of something specific. What is it?\""
    },
