      "narrative": "Mara's mug hits the table harder than she meant it to \u2014 a clunk that draws a glance from Toran at the bar. She holds your gaze, but something in her posture stiffens.\n\n\"By name?\" She repeats, and there's a flatness to her voice now, a wall going up. \"Old Bram was the ferryman. Everyone knew that. You'd find him at the Gate at dusk, and if you had coin and he had the inclination, he'd take you through. That's how it worked.\"\n\nShe picks at a splinter in the table's edge, not meeting your eyes now.\n\n\"Look, I don't know what you're digging for, but you're scratching at dirt that's already been turned. Bram's dead. Gate's locked. Toran built it. That's the whole list of names I've got.\"\n\nShe stops picking at the wood. Her fingers go still.\n\n\"And frankly? You're starting to sound like you think I'm holding back on you. I'm not.\" A beat. \"I just don't *have* more names to give.\"\n\nThe silence that follows is heavy. Toran clears his throat at the bar and busies himself wiping a glass that's already dry."
    },
