      "narrative": "The name hangs in the still air for a moment \u2014 \"Old Bram!\" \u2014 then fades against the empty hill beyond the arch. No echo. The shimmer in the Gate's frame ripples once, like disturbed water settling.\n\nThen you catch it.\n\nA faint rustle. Dry, papery \u2014 like someone shifting in a bed of dead leaves. It comes from *behind* the Gate. From somewhere on the other side of that shimmer, where the hill rises.\n\nAnd then \u2014 a voice. Muffled, indistinct, as if speaking through a heavy cloth or from deep underground. You can't make out words, only the shape of them: a single phrase, maybe two, rising and falling like a question.\n\nThen silence. The rustle stops. Whatever was there has gone still.\n\nThe stained earth at your feet holds its dark stain. The iron wheel glints with fresh oil. The gate shimmers, dormant, unopened."
    },
