      "narrative": "You drop to a crouch, running your fingers through the dark, scuffed earth where Old Bram's body was found. The soil is loose on top, compacted beneath \u2014 boot prints, drag marks, the general disturbance of a death scene days old. You sift through it, turning over pebbles and bits of grit, brushing aside a crushed leaf, checking for anything \u2014 a scrap of cloth, a dropped coin, a mark carved into the dirt.\n\nNothing.\n\nJust earth. Just stains. Just the shape of where a man fell and was carried away.\n\nYou straighten, dirt clinging to your palms, and the silence presses in around you. The shimmer in the Gate's arch holds steady. The hill beyond it looks no different than it did a moment ago.\n\nNo voice answers your question. No hidden thing reveals itself.\n\nThe stained earth offers nothing but the fact of itself \u2014 dark, scuffed, empty."
